{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CesvuhMLyQSpJD4Ba8mLS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Repo has an empty `intent/` directory, so this will be `intent/0001-<slug>/intent.md`.\n\nBefore I write it: the skill's rule is that Problem carries observed facts in your words, and anything nobody can answer stays an open question rather than getting invented. So a few questions — skip any you don't have, and I'll record those as open questions with a name attached.\n\n**Problem facts**\n1. \"A third of every call\" — is that measured (call QA, ticket tags, handle-time data) or the team's impression? Any numbers: calls/week, average handle time, what share of calls are status-only?\n2. What kind of claims are these — insurance, warranty, expenses, something else?\n\n**Scope**\n3. What does a customer need to see to stop calling? Just a status label, or the timeline of what's happened, or \"what happens next / when\"?\n4. Anything explicitly *out*? For example: documents, adjuster notes, payment amounts, the ability to message the adjuster.\n\n**Users and systems**\n5. Which customers — everyone with a portal login, or a subset (policyholders only, not brokers/agents)?\n6. Who else is touched that you haven't mentioned? Specifically: do adjusters or claims handlers write internal statuses that would now become customer-visible?\n\n**Constraints**\n7. Are there claim states that must *not* be shown externally — fraud review, litigation, subrogation, that kind of thing?\n8. Portal auth: is there an existing login customers already use for this, or is that an open item?\n\n**Success**\n9. What would make you say this worked, in a sentence you could check in three months? (\"Status-only calls drop below X\" is the kind of thing I mean.)\n\nAnswer what you can and I'll draft it; you'll get the file to correct before anything is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details